WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:23.750
(flatulence)

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.430
Welcome back to Things You Missed.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:29.320
I know it’s been a while since you’ve
seen me; I did not upload last week, so you’ve

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.859
probably forgotten who I am.

00:00:30.859 --> 00:00:35.390
My name is CZ and it’s my job to analyse
horror movies for any content you may have

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:36.390
missed.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:41.300
Today I’m gonna be covering Slenderman…
or I guess Slender Man is the actual title

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.850
of this movie, like there’s a space there
for some reason.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:48.010
Perhaps to foreshadow the fact that this movie
would contain a lot of empty filler.

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:51.750
But despite Sony’s product placement of
their Xperia phones being the highest level

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:55.860
of effort put into this movie, I do have a
theory about the meaning of what we saw on

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:57.900
screen, or at least what they were going for.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:01.890
And I do think this theory will be worth your
time, more so than the film itself, so be

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:03.410
sure to stick around for that.

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:07.740
Let’s start by going back to 6 months ago,
when the trailer for Slender Man first came

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:10.580
out, and I being CZsWorld, did a Things You
Missed on it.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:15.290
One of the Things I noticed was there didn’t
seem to be any ties to the established lore

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:18.990
of Slenderman, from the original photos to
Marble Hornets, to the symbology we’ve come

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:20.700
to associate with Slenderman.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.810
This led me to believe that this could be
drawing more inspiration from the real life

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:27.530
incident known as “The Slenderman Stabbing”,
when two girls tried to kill their friend

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:31.290
with a knife, supposedly with the belief that
they were making a sacrifice to Slenderman.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:35.380
Slenderman, of course, does not exist, and
these girls were mentally ill.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:39.350
They allowed this viral creepypasta story
to alter their perception of reality, and

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:42.140
an innocent girl almost paid the ultimate
price for it.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:43.579
I’m gonna go out of order here.

00:01:43.579 --> 00:01:45.630
Let’s skip to the last line of the movie.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:49.670
The voiceover compares the spreading of the
Slender sickness to something going viral.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:52.560
It also mentions that some take it too far
and try to summon Slenderman.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:56.580
The movie is comparing the mental illness
of these girls to the viral takeover of a

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:00.840
popular creepypasta, and there are plenty
of examples of evidence throughout the movie.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:02.490
So let’s go through them.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:03.490
Exhibit A.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:07.700
The Slender sickness spreads quickly through
the internet, just like the creepypasta.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:11.400
The very first scene of the movie shows two
of the girls watching a viral video of a breakdancing

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.710
cat on their phones.

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:15.910
One of them mentions that she’d like the
video better if the cat were to explode.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:20.040
Right off the bat, we are shown the influence
of viral memes on their life, and how it can

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.330
make some of them take things too far.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:25.510
Then, that night when they’re hanging out
in Katie’s basement, they first find out

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:29.510
about Slenderman from a rumor that their guy
friends are going to try to summon him, so

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:31.060
they decide to try it themselves.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.840
They watch the video, it causes them to have
some kind of vision, and they describe a weird

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:35.900
feeling coming over all of them.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:40.260
I see that as them getting the virus, getting
the mental illness in their head.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:44.230
After Katie’s disappearance, the girls recover
her laptop, and find that she’s been browsing

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.370
all of these Slenderman websites.

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:51.820
She had been on these forums with posts from
users named Mchylr, Sabby99, Paulyyy with

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:53.740
three Ys and Aleekat93.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:58.879
They would later find out that Aleekat93 is
one of the last people that Katie spoke with

00:02:58.879 --> 00:03:03.340
online before her disappearance, and towards
the end of the movie they discover that Aleekat93

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:07.060
is actually a girl named Allison Riley, a
mental patient.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:10.989
This is enough to at least suspect that the
mental illness, Slender sickness, whatever

00:03:10.989 --> 00:03:14.740
you want to call it is literally passed from
person to person online, and it’s later

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:21.290
confirmed when Wren decides to message Alliekat93
and it leads her to go insane; sounding like

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:26.290
a complete nutcase when trying to describe
some bio-electric aura garbage to Hallie,

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:30.569
drawing a huge amount of pictures of Slenderman,
and standing at the edge of her window contemplating

00:03:30.569 --> 00:03:31.569
suicide.

00:03:31.569 --> 00:03:34.840
If you’re not convinced, look back at the
scene where Wren describes the nature of the

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:37.210
virus after first talking to Aleekat93.

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:41.400
I mean, don’t literally watch the movie
again, that would be awful, but just think

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.690
back to that scene.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:46.450
Wren describes the sickness as a virus that
gets in your head, and uses the comparison

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.870
of a computer virus, but in your brain.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:53.800
Why would she use a computer virus as a reference
point, as opposed to an actual medical virus?

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:57.120
I’m pretty sure a computer virus is only
called a virus, because it’s similar to

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.290
an actual virus you might contract.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:03.190
So her wording is weird on that, but it makes
sense going back to the comparison with the

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:06.989
real-life Slenderman stabbing girls, because
they essentially made themselves mentally

00:04:06.989 --> 00:04:11.600
ill by visiting these websites from a young
age and convincing themselves that Slenderman

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:12.610
somehow exists.

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:17.610
So that brings me to Exhibit B. Once you have
the disease, it causes destructive behaviour.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:21.220
At the beginning of the movie they all have
their own dreams, and by the end, they’ve

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:23.070
effectively sabotaged those dreams.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.490
A question is posed to the group early on.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:26.530
“OK Twitter poll.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:30.320
If you could stay one age forever, what would
it be?”

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:33.560
Each of their answers tells us something about
that character.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:34.800
Let’s start with Katie.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:35.800
She says 21.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:39.840
That could be because she sees her alcoholic
father and thinks drinking away her sorrows

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.919
is the only way to deal with her miserable
life.

00:04:41.919 --> 00:04:45.030
She’s always going on about being stuck
in this town she hates.

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:47.910
And it’s on her computer that the video
is originally watched.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:51.680
I think she actually kind of wants to summon
Slenderman and wants to be taken away by him

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:52.790
because she’s depressed.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:56.680
So she’s the first one to become mentally
ill, and she’s basically the one to pass

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:58.620
it onto the other girls.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:04:59.699
You could also argue that it starts with her
father.

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:04.000
I don’t know if being an alcoholic counts,
but he does seem disturbed when he breaks

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:08.030
into Hallie’s house, where he mentions that
Katie was never into this occult stuff before

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:09.030
she disappeared.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:12.870
How would he even know about that without
knowing about the whole Slenderman ritual?

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:16.460
Also, when the girls sneak into Katie’s
room to recover the laptop, the dad can be

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:21.000
seen watching TV with his usual bottle of
alcohol, but he also now has pill bottles,

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.690
which leads me to believe that at this point
in the movie, he too has the Slender sickness.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:28.460
But going back to Katie, they look through
her computer and if you look at her desktop

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:33.509
icons there are folders labeled, homework
(pretty self-explanatory), project hometown

00:05:33.509 --> 00:05:36.720
(which I’m guessing is part of her plan
to get out of her hometown as mentioned near

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:40.449
the beginning of the movie), and a folder
called ideas looks (which I’m not sure what

00:05:40.449 --> 00:05:44.240
that is, but the ideas portion could have
something to do with the fact that Slenderman

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:45.800
gets in your head, much like an idea.)

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:50.570
There are also two files seen on her desktop,
one called “founder of the…” dot dot

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:52.800
dot, and the other named bucket list.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:57.009
I don’t know too many 16 year olds who already
have a bucket list, and I’m guessing that

00:05:57.009 --> 00:05:58.960
is not there for positive reasons.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:03.680
So looking at all of this, it seems like Katie
wants escape town and her alcoholic dad, but

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:07.210
the contraction of the illness leads her to
a more destructive path towards getting out

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:08.229
of her current life.

00:06:08.229 --> 00:06:10.419
Chloe’s response to the “what age would
you want to be?”

00:06:10.419 --> 00:06:11.930
question is nine years old.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:14.830
This is probably because her dad died in the
military when she was nine.

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:17.772
It’s kind of implied, because when they
go to make a sacrifice in the woods to try

00:06:17.772 --> 00:06:21.449
get Katie back, she sacrifices the last picture
of her and her Dad.

00:06:21.449 --> 00:06:25.139
And later on when we are seeing Slenderman’s
POV through Chloe’s house, you can spot

00:06:25.139 --> 00:06:27.389
of picture of her Dad wearing military gear.

00:06:27.389 --> 00:06:31.710
We don’t really know what she does to sabotage
her dream, because she kind of stops being

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:34.270
in the movie for the most part after seeing
Slenderman.

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:37.460
You may have figured this out by now but this
is not a perfect movie, but I’m just going

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:40.800
to try to give you as much information as
I can, and you can always let me know your

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.389
own thoughts in the comments.

00:06:42.389 --> 00:06:46.210
Moving on to Wren, she said she would want
to remain 30 years old, and she specifically

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:49.319
cites that 30 is the age when you’re most
mentally stable.

00:06:49.319 --> 00:06:53.110
Wren ends up being the one who is the least
mentally stable, having crazy delusions in

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:57.289
the library and really just sounding like
a complete crazy person in her speech and

00:06:57.289 --> 00:06:59.240
being pushed to the brink of suicide.

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:02.539
So that just leaves the main girl, Hallie,
who says she’d like to remain the same age

00:07:02.539 --> 00:07:03.539
that she is right now.

00:07:03.539 --> 00:07:04.539
She has a good life.

00:07:04.539 --> 00:07:07.289
She loves her sister and she’s a track star
at her school.

00:07:07.289 --> 00:07:09.030
You can see some of her trophies above her
bed.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:12.919
Early on, her sister brings up the fact that
one of her teammates quit the track team after

00:07:12.919 --> 00:07:17.289
getting pregnant, and this establishes Hallie’s
fear of growing up and taking on those adult

00:07:17.289 --> 00:07:18.460
responsibilities.

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:20.640
So what does the Slenderman sickness do to
her?

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:24.669
It gives her a vision of herself getting pregnant
and the sickness then spreads to her sister,

00:07:24.669 --> 00:07:28.470
and she has to give up the life that she loves
in order to try to protect Lizzie.

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:33.009
Like the Slenderman Stabbing girls from 2014,
the girls in this movie engage in some destructive

00:07:33.009 --> 00:07:35.650
behaviors once Slenderman gets in their head.

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:38.919
Exhibit C. Once you see it, you can’t unsee
it.

00:07:38.919 --> 00:07:42.050
This line basically tells us that there is
no cure for the Slender sickness.

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:45.819
And once the characters have the virus, they
start seeing the symbols of facelessness and

00:07:45.819 --> 00:07:47.050
eyelessness everywhere.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:51.099
The original idea for the logo of Slenderman,
which I don't think appears in this movie

00:07:51.099 --> 00:07:55.530
anywhere, is that it's a head with the face
crossed out because Slenderman has no face.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:59.509
So it looks like that idea is kind of kept
in fact, only in this movie it's specifically

00:07:59.509 --> 00:08:01.419
no eyes as opposed to no face.

00:08:01.419 --> 00:08:05.240
The legend that they read before watching
the video tells them to keep their eyes closed

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:06.240
and their minds open.

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:10.521
A bunch of images flash on the screen, some
of which look like Illuminati symbols, but

00:08:10.521 --> 00:08:13.120
I'm guessing they’re just supposed to be
like eye symbols.

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:16.699
There are also some letters and numbers that
are briefly flashed on screen.

00:08:16.699 --> 00:08:20.300
It looks kind of like programming language,
and further ties into the comparison between

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:22.479
Slender sickness and a computer virus.

00:08:22.479 --> 00:08:26.550
After watching the video when they have their
visions of the forest or whatever is going

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:29.830
on there, there are some jump cuts of a girl
with a melting face.

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:33.770
After recovering Katie's laptop and browsing
the Slenderman websites, for some reason you

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:38.300
can see the HTML code of the sites, and the
words “You see him” are hidden periodically

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:42.100
throughout the HTML, which didn't really make
much sense, but it does fit in with the eye

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:43.979
or lack of eyes motif.

00:08:43.979 --> 00:08:47.180
When Wren is researching in the library, she
comes across this photo.

00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:51.490
If you don't know what it is, it's the original
photo from the Something Awful forums photoshop

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:55.470
contest that started the whole Slenderman
phenomenon in 2009.

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:56.850
“IT’S 2009!”

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:59.130
This is where the character was born.

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:02.630
So it's cool to see the photo making a cameo
in the movie, but when it appears in the movie,

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:05.339
all of the eyes of the human characters are
crossed out.

00:09:05.339 --> 00:09:09.170
It's probably for copyright reasons, but again
it does kind of fit in with the eyeless motif.

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:12.560
In Hallie’s science class they are studying
and dissecting corneas.

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:16.740
And when Hallie and Wren go to check up on
Chloe at her some, she has this empty blank

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:17.910
look in her eyes.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:21.529
Wren has some drawings of crossed out eyes
in her room, and the hospital is filled with

00:09:21.529 --> 00:09:25.760
eyeless and faceless characters, like some
Grandma who's eyes disappear, a doctor with

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:29.730
no eyes and the lady getting her hair combed
who had no face.

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:34.570
When Hallie’s little sister Lizzie has her…
medical emergency that’s never really explained,

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:39.350
we see flashes of maggots, which are little
fly larvae that often make their homes in

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:43.880
rotting flesh such as the eyes, and then Lizzie
wakes up screaming “he had no face.”

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:48.300
And then in the final scene with Hallie, where
she is chased by Slenderman doing his best

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:52.830
Doc Oc impersonation, she ends up at the tree
from her original vision where the vines grow

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:55.950
over her entire body, and the last thing they
cover is her eyes.

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:59.589
There are probably many more that you can
catch, so let me know what you saw in the

00:09:59.589 --> 00:10:00.589
comments.

00:10:00.589 --> 00:10:06.770
That brings me to my last Exhibit: Exhibit
D. Slenderman doesn’t actually exist.

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:10.529
Just like Slenderman was merely a delusion
of the real life Slenderman Stabbing girls,

00:10:10.529 --> 00:10:14.730
there's evidence in the movie to suggest that
the girls are the only ones who see or even

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:18.370
know about Slenderman, with the possible exception
of Katie’s dad.

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:21.730
At the beginning of the movie, the guys are
stated to have some secret plans for the night.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:24.959
Chloe later claims that they were planning
on summoning Slenderman, which is where the

00:10:24.959 --> 00:10:27.040
girls get the idea that they’re gonna do
it too.

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:30.490
However, there isn't any evidence that the
guys actually do it.

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:33.120
Nothing happens to anyone in town outside
the four girls.

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:36.540
None of the guys make any mention of Slenderman
throughout the movie.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:40.470
When Hallie hangs out with Tom and brings
up the video, he acts like he's never seen

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:41.470
it before.

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:45.310
The first supposed “Slenderman encounter
scene turns out to just be Katie's dad breaking

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:47.019
into Hallie and Lizzie’s house.

00:10:47.019 --> 00:10:51.070
When Slenderman supposedly breaks into Chloe’s
house and attacks her, at the end of the scene

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:56.550
the camera pans to the mirror to reveal Chloe
is choking herself and Slenderman isn't actually

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:57.550
even there.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:00.649
When Tom is asking out Hallie after school,
she keeps looking over to the woods where

00:11:00.649 --> 00:11:04.330
she can see Slenderman, but Tom can't seem
to notice anything out of the ordinary.

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:08.420
If I'm not mistaken, I think all the actual
sightings of Slenderman are seen through the

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:11.839
perspective of the four girls who to try to
summon him at the beginning of the movie,

00:11:11.839 --> 00:11:15.360
at least until the sickness is passed off
to Lizzie later in the movie.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:18.980
So those are my four exhibits on how this
movie is trying to compare the Slender sickness

00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:20.720
to real mental illness.

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:23.900
There were a few other Things I Missed that
I thought you might be interested in hearing

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:24.900
about.

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:26.640
There seem to be some link between Hallie
and Slenderman.

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:31.269
The character they communicate with to learn
more about Slenderman goes by Aleekat93, or

00:11:31.269 --> 00:11:32.269
Alee.

00:11:32.269 --> 00:11:35.600
It sounds very similar to the protagonist
Hallie, which wouldn’t be significant if

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:39.190
not for the fact that Alee is never shown
and seems to have all the information about

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:40.190
Slenderman.

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:44.180
Then the movie seems to suggest that Hallie
is absorbed by Slenderman or something at

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:47.601
the end, because she gets engulfed by that
tree, and shortly before that there’s a

00:11:47.601 --> 00:11:52.220
shot where she walks behind a tree and briefly
becomes Slenderman for a moment, before crossing

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:54.650
by another tree and returning to normal.

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:58.180
And then near the beginning of the movie when
the girls are all hanging out in Katie’s

00:11:58.180 --> 00:12:02.980
basement, when we come into the scene they
are all talking about porn, as girls do, and

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:06.630
they are specifically talking about watching
POV porn from the girl’s point of view…

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:10.500
and I guess that has something to do with
those scenes later on where Slenderman video

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:14.230
calls them and we see him sneaking into their
houses from his POV.

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:17.750
Not sure if that was necessary, but just thought
I’d point out that comparison.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:20.720
It really is quite ironic about Slenderman.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:24.040
He started out as a contest entry on the Something
Awful forums.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:28.670
And now in 2018, they truly have made something
awful.

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:32.470
Now if you’ll excuse me, I think I’m gonna
go watch Eighth Grade a third time to cleanse

